{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the sense is: then all will recognize and know that everyone who builds upon a burnt-offering [עולה] will not be saved by it; when the day of his calamity comes, then he will trust in HaShem and know His ways."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Read בעולה literally as 'upon a burnt-offering'; possibly a play on עול (iniquity), but translated hyper-literally as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:51.534982339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}